# FIX-BLACK regression: a client whose LOCAL house is not 0 (a network joiner,
# or the L2 debug switch `set local_house 1`) must see its own base: terrain
# drawn under the local house's shroud (not house 0's), the camera opening on
# its start, its own units on screen. (User report: "the second player has a
# black map" -- iso_renderer drew terrain through house 0's explored mask.)
set render_every 60
set on_quit continue
set humans 0,1
set local_house 1

click button "Single Player"
click button Skirmish
require scene == lobby
click combo:country1
click list:down
click list:down
click list:down
click pick:Russia
click start
until 90 scene == game
require scene == game
assert local_house == 1
wait 60
shot local1_f60
dump
assert local_explored > 100
assert local_explored_on_screen > 100
assert terrain_drawn > 200
assert own_on_screen >= 1
assert cam_own_dist < 15
wait 240
shot local1_f300
dump
assert local_explored_on_screen > 100
assert terrain_drawn > 200
assert own_on_screen >= 1
end
